Detection logic was developed around security-relevant endpoint activity and mapped to MITRE ATT&CK techniques.

Examples include:

Detection	MITRE ATT&CK
PowerShell execution	T1059.001
Windows Command Shell	T1059.003
Encoded PowerShell	T1027 / T1059.001
Failed authentication	T1110
Network/service discovery	T1046
LSASS access	T1003.001
Scheduled task activity	T1053.005
Suspicious network connection	Technique-dependent
Malware/hash-based detection	Technique-dependent

Detection development includes:

Detection Logic → MITRE Mapping → Severity → False Positives → Investigation → Response
